 * CHANGELOG
 *
 * 24-10-2026 (0.3.0)
 *
 * Modernization for current systems and IRCNet 2.11+/2.12.0-pre:
 * - Native 64-bit builds by default (optional --with-32bit)
 * - OpenSSL SSL/TLS support (--with-ssl / auto-detect, port 6697)
 * - Updated configure.sh: better platform support (Linux, macOS, FreeBSD, SunOS, Cygwin)
 * - GitHub Actions CI: Ubuntu, macOS, FreeBSD
 * - Code hygiene: vsnprintf, time.h, abs() fix, key.h dependency
 * - Keep full backward compatibility with plain TCP and old servers
 * - Binary validator remains optional (--without-validator)
 *
 * 13-01-2014 (0.2.3)
 *
 * improved clones loading system
 * now when single clone load to fail, program will no exit, just report it
 *
 * added dynamic clones loading system (not tested very well)
 * new command: load - connect given number of clones (but still suggest to load clones using parameter in command line)
 *
 * simplified usage again (./cloner <server> [port] [number] [delay] [ip vhost file])
 * when port not given use default
 *
 * added defines:
 * default server port: 6667
 * default clones loading number (when not given): 0 (mean no auto loading from command line, when no parameter)
 *
 * 13-01-2014 (0.2.2-2)
 *
 * disable ip check while accepting incomming connection for built-in ident service
 * added "no-ident" file check (if exists, cloner will not try to use built-in ident service)
 *
 * added defines:
 * default no ident file: .no-ident
 *
 * 03-01-2014 (0.2.2-1)
 *
 * added auto-rejoin check (if clones are not channels, they will try to join every 20 secs)
 * improved register nick with ircd (if fail to register generated nick, clones will use unique ID)
 * 
 * 01-01-2014 (0.2.2)
 *
 * fixed bug with auto-entering neutral mode on channel join (clones didn't react when opped)
 * fixed bug with auto-exit program when nickname was already in use (while registering to ircd)
 *
 * improved debug mode 
 * logging all parsed data to file for every clone connection
 * new command: neutral - print information about current mode (if on, clones will not react when opped)
 *              this should simplify debuging accidently auto-entering neutral mode 
 *
 * 31-12-2013 (0.2.1-1)
 *
 * improved user commands (cosmetic adjustments)
 * help  - join with delay information
 * chan  - will show chan if already set
 * key   - will show chan key if already set
 * addop - now check if nick is not already added.
 *         if try to add mask (nick!user@host), will extract nick from mask and add nick only.
 *
 * 31-12-2013 (0.2.1)
 *
 * added ipv6 support for built-in ident server
 * tested ipv6 vhost (using ::1 as vhost (local ip) and seems working)
 *
 * 30-12-2013 (0.2.0-1)
 *
 * added built-in ident server (ipv4 only)
 * will work only, if process got permission to bind on port lower than 1024 (by default root only)
 * and port is not already in use (mean no oidentd service running). if want to use this feature, run 
 * cloner as root and kill oidentd service before (killall -9 oidentd).
 *
 * 26-12-2013 (0.2.0)
 *
 * fixed vhost loading (not tested for ipv6, ipv4 tested) 
 * fixed corrupted memory data parsing crash 
 * added simple binary protector
 * added configure script
 * added creating relase scripts
 *
 * added defines
 * internal clone buffer size: 1024 chars
 *
 * 13-12-2013 (0.1.0-2)
 *
 * improved vhost loading function
 * now will check, if a line is valid ip (or ipv6) address 
 *
 * added chan key support
 *
 * added joining chan with delay
 *
 * 12-12-2013 (0.1.0-1)
 *
 * added ipv6 support
 *
 * added vhost support
 * 
 * simplified usage
 * 
 * added defines
 * ipv6 support: yes
 * default vhost file: .vhosts
 * default connect delay: 1 sec
 * 
 * 11-12-2013 (0.1.0)
 * 
 * improved work algorithm
 * instead of first op all clones, then start deoping, we will mix those actions.
 * if there is someone to punish, and other clone to op, will first op max other 2 
 * other clones and punish other 3 or 4 (depends of mode) of enemies. such algorithm 
 * improve efficiency rate when using kick mode (4-5% efficiency increase). 
 * it's also interrupt (in most cases) algorithm of defensive botnet's and scripts
 * which are protecting channel.
 *
 * added random nick support
 *
 * added defines
 * channel max length: 50 chars
 * nick max length: 15 chars
 * max clones: 100
 * lag check delay: 30 secs
 * max connect delay: 1 day
